{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch-sonnet5/runs/eval-INC-86-r1-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "Confirmed — `npm test` fails pre-existingly (unrelated to this fix), and `npm run check` is the correct command; it passes all 27 tests with my changes.\n\nFixed INC-86: `primaryClass` in `src/cargo/hazmat.ts:13-19` was truncating every hazard division to the digit before the dot (e.g. `\"5.1\"` → `\"5\"`), so oxidisers, organic peroxides, and other divisioned classes never matched the segregation table. Now only class 1 (explosives) divisions collapse to `\"1\"`; other classes keep their full division. Updated `test/hazmat.test.ts` to match correct behavior and added cases mirroring the incident's acceptance criteria. `npm run check` passes (27/27).", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9WeJZHRtf98Qn6M4BT", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "42b9cd29-6efe-42f7-8d0c-080bf98da21d", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:43:43.811Z", "type": "assistant"}
